    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class with `@Test` methods; the other two files are the abstract `AcceptanceBase` and a support class).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipTier` derived field with minimal structural impact by mirroring the existing computed-field pattern (`membershipNumber`, `displayName`, etc.) rather than growing any method or class:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipTier` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` expression on the existing `toOwnerDto` method:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(Integer.valueOf(0).equals(owner.getNamesakeCount()) && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \\\"SILVER\\\" : \\\"BRONZE\\\")\")\n   ```\n\nThe logic returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and a non-blank email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`. Both acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass, and the build is green.",
